# L §2.5 Keys at a stepped range (tally 2.1.7 B1, issue #150; G12): a day range's values are a + i·s from a, so
# 9999-10-31 .. 9999-12-31 step 1 month holds 9999-12-31, and a key's membership never steps past the last day
# there is: 9999-11-30 is read, 9999-12-01 is refused with RUN-KEY's form. 2.1.6's refcore refused RUN-LIMIT `a day
# passes 9999-12-31`.
=== g12.tally
model g12
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "made up"

input fee[d in 9999-10-31 .. 9999-12-31 step 1 month]: num

input at_day: date

ask q_on: fee[at_day]

ask q_off: fee[at_day + 1 day]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  fee[9999-10-31] = 1 "the card"
  fee[9999-11-30] = 2 "the card"
  fee[9999-12-31] = 3 "the card"
  at_day = 9999-11-30 "the card"
=== expect
q_off: refused: RUN-KEY 9999-12-01 is not a value of 9999-10-31 .. 9999-12-31 step 1 month
  cut 2026-03-01
q_on: 2
  cut 2026-03-01
